1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,680
Lights drifting between the graves, on a

2
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:04,731
hill northeast of LaPorte, near Hesston.

3
00:00:04,961 --> 00:00:06,865
This is Posey Chapel Cemetery.

4
00:00:07,415 --> 00:00:10,449
In 1841, settlers from the surrounding

5
00:00:10,459 --> 00:00:12,170
farms built a log chapel here.

6
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,740
Local history says it was the first church

7
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:16,001
in Galena Township.

8
00:00:16,401 --> 00:00:18,229
They named it for the circuit preacher who

9
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:20,510
urged them to build it, Wade Posey.

10
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:23,867
In 1855, a new chapel replaced the log

11
00:00:23,877 --> 00:00:24,121
one.

12
00:00:24,571 --> 00:00:26,223
It stood for more than a century.

13
00:00:26,453 --> 00:00:30,543
Then, on the night of January 26, 1972,

14
00:00:30,553 --> 00:00:33,223
arsonists set it on fire, and it burned to

15
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:33,662
the ground.

16
00:00:34,412 --> 00:00:36,739
Today, a pavilion stands where the chapel

17
00:00:36,749 --> 00:00:37,011
was.

18
00:00:37,461 --> 00:00:39,672
Visitors report glowing lights among the

19
00:00:39,682 --> 00:00:41,938
stones, and sounds they can't explain.

20
00:00:42,788 --> 00:00:44,089
It's a real cemetery.

21
00:00:44,319 --> 00:00:46,159
Please visit in daylight, and be

22
00:00:46,169 --> 00:00:46,702
respectful.

23
00:00:47,202 --> 00:00:49,245
Comment your town, and it could be next.

